{
  "reviewed": true,
  "theme": "cassette",
  "notes": "Issue #30, fifth package; same decisions as breaker, rate, cache and retry (see scm/docs/package-layout-migration-map.md). -api: CassetteConfig and CassetteConfigBuilder (schema, defaults, TOML parsing, builder), CassetteError, DTOs, the Processor, Validator and HttpCassette traits, and the new CassetteFactory and CassetteLayer contract traits. -std: the record/replay middleware (fixture store, body scrubber, recorded interactions, request matching) behind StdCassetteFactory; every concrete type is crate-private. The public CassetteLayer was a concrete struct that carried the reqwest-middleware impl, and an impl of a foreign trait must live in the crate that defines the type, so the struct moves to -std as the private FileCassetteLayer and CassetteLayer becomes a contract trait (Middleware + HttpCassette + Debug); the factory returns Arc<dyn CassetteLayer>. CassetteLayerBuilder (with_config, with_cassette_name, build_layer) is dropped: CassetteFactory::build_cassette_layer(config, name) is its replacement and needs no second construction path. api/body, api/recorded, api/default, api/cassette and api/processor held only placeholder type aliases and empty modules (most were not even compiled); they are dropped.",
